%erg 0.1
Title: Add make check alias (test + validate) to align with the pre-PR gate
Created: 2026-06-03
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-06-03T00:30Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

git-erg has no `make check` target, yet the cross-project convention (and
the exit criteria of tickets 0210, 0211, 0213 and 0214, which say "make
check passe"; 0212 says "make test passe") expect `make check` to be the
pre-PR gate. Today the real gate is `make test` + `erg check tickets/`.
The verify-gate on PR #245 (ticket 0210) ESCALATED solely because criterion
"make check passe" could not be satisfied -- there is no such target.
Adding a thin alias makes that criterion literally true (no goalpost-moving)
and clears it across the 4-series at once. This is the verify-gate's own
recommendation.

## Actions

1. Add a `.PHONY` `check` target to the Makefile that runs the real gate:
   `check: test validate` (test = Go unit + shell suites; validate = the
   existing target that runs `erg check tickets/`).
2. Add `check` to the Makefile usage comment header.
3. Update CONTRIBUTING.md's "make test is the gate" line to note that
   `make check` is the alias (so docs stay honest).

## Test

Source-inspection guard (no slow subprocess): a check that the Makefile
defines a `check:` target with `test` and `validate` prerequisites, and
that `check` is in `.PHONY`. Fold into the existing `tests/test_docs.sh`
rather than adding a new suite.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make check` runs `make test` and `make validate` (the real gate).
- [ ] `check` is `.PHONY` (it produces no output file).
- [ ] Makefile usage header lists `make check`.
- [ ] CONTRIBUTING.md notes the alias.
- [ ] `make test` passes.
